  "sourceNotes": "Coconut-based layer cakes are well established in Caribbean and South Asian baking traditions, as well as in the American Southern baking canon (coconut cake with seven-minute frosting). The addition of mango as a filling reflects the influence of South Asian and Caribbean flavour traditions in British home baking from the 2010s onward. The specific format, coconut sponge, fresh mango curd or puree filling, coconut frosting, became a recognisable style in UK celebration baking after appearing in competition baking shows and food magazines from about 2014.",
