          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bake the coconut sponge layers"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Preheat the oven to 180°C conventional (160°C fan). Grease and line three 20 cm round tins. Cream the butter and sugar together until pale and fluffy. Beat in the eggs one at a time. Fold in the flour, desiccated coconut, and baking powder alternately with the coconut milk in three additions. Divide evenly among the tins and bake for 25 to 28 minutes until a skewer comes out clean. Cool completely before assembling."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the mango filling and frosting"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Blitz the mango flesh with the lime juice until smooth. Taste, the puree should be sharp and fruity. If it's too watery, simmer briefly in a small pan to thicken. Set aside to cool. For the frosting: beat the butter and cream cheese together until smooth. Add the icing sugar in two batches, beating well, then add the coconut extract."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assemble with a mango dam"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Place the first sponge on a board. Pipe a ring of frosting around the outer edge to contain the filling. Spread half the mango filling inside the ring. Add the second layer and repeat. Place the final layer on top. Apply a crumb coat of frosting, refrigerate for 20 minutes, then apply the final coat. Press toasted coconut flakes around the sides and over the top before the frosting sets."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
